    {
      "term": "Sengoku Unification",
      "matchText": "Sengoku Unification",
      "definition": "The fifty-year process (roughly 1560–1615) by which three successive warlords — Oda Nobunaga, Toyotomi Hideyoshi, and Tokugawa Ieyasu — reassembled the warring states of Sengoku Japan into a single state. As much a gunpowder revolution as a political one, it ended with the Tokugawa shogunate and the long Edo peace.",
      "type": "concept"
    },
