    {
      "term": "Eastern Army",
      "matchText": "Eastern Army",
      "definition": "The coalition Tokugawa Ieyasu led at Sekigahara in 1600 — mostly daimyo from the Kantō and northeastern Honshu, joined by western lords with grudges against Ishida Mitsunari. Its victory made the Tokugawa masters of Japan.",
      "type": "concept"
    },
    {
      "term": "Western Army",
      "matchText": "Western Army",
      "definition": "The coalition Ishida Mitsunari assembled at Sekigahara — daimyo from western Honshu, Shikoku, and Kyushu, nominally fighting for Hideyoshi's young heir. Defections during the battle, above all Kobayakawa Hideaki's, broke it within hours.",
      "type": "concept"
