      "matchText": "Nakano Dog Kennels",
      "type": "place",
      "definition": "The vast public dog shelter built northwest of Edo under Tokugawa Tsunayoshi to house the city's strays after his Edicts of Compassion for Living Beings made killing or abandoning dogs a crime. At its height it held an estimated 50,000 dogs, fed rice, fish, and miso paid for out of the shogunate treasury — the most expensive symbol of the policies that earned Tsunayoshi the nickname Dog Shogun."
